# Performance Rules

## Code splitting
- Every page is lazy-loaded: `React.lazy(() => import('./Page'))`.
- Wrap lazy pages with `<Suspense fallback={<PageSkeleton />}>` in the router.
- Heavy third-party libs (charts, editors, PDF) are dynamic-imported at the usage site.

## Renders
- Never create objects or arrays inline in JSX props — `useMemo` or module-level const.
- Never define functions inline in JSX props passed to memoised children — `useCallback`.
- Zustand: subscribe to slices, never the whole store object.
- React Query: use `select` to return only the data the component needs.

## Bundle
- Keep initial JS bundle under 200 KB gzipped.
- Tree-shake: import named exports, never `import _ from 'lodash'`.
- Analyse with `vite-bundle-visualizer` before each release.

## Images
- All images have explicit `width` and `height`.
- Use `loading="lazy"` on below-the-fold images.
- SVGs used as icons are inlined as React components (vite-plugin-svgr).
